      "dom_id": "question-904",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find $|z|$ if $z=-c-d\\text{i},$ where $c$ and $d$ are real numbers.",
      "worked_solution": "For a complex number $z=a+b\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFor the complex number $z=-c-d\\text{i},$ we have $a=-c$ and $b=-d.$ So, the magnitude is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}|-c-d\\text{i}| & =\\sqrt{(-c)^{2}+(-d)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{c}^{2}+{d}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
